{"title":"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Infinite\" title=\"Infinite\">infinite</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometric_series\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Geometric series\">geometric series</a> has sum 2005. A new series, obtained by squaring each term of the original series, has 10 times the sum of the original series. The common <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ratio\" title=\"Ratio\">ratio</a> of the original series is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/9/9b9ffa9646e74f6e94a4a66b824c3a3f08f4f4b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac mn$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"18\" height=\"33\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Relatively_prime\" title=\"Relatively prime\">relatively prime</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integers</a>. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db26f75f6218a382840f0ed34f5d36bcff61d33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's call the first term of the original <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometric_series\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Geometric series\">geometric series</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and the common ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/1/4b1471ee6c3db64b0d92179e503c2f0231f7e754.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2005 = a + ar + ar^2 + \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"200\" height=\"16\" />.  Using the sum formula for <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Infinite\" title=\"Infinite\">infinite</a> geometric series, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/e/a5ec59dfe65a976d7dbcf40af85b0f1e8911e8ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\;\\;\\frac a{1 -r} = 2005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"117\" height=\"36\" />.  Then we form a new series, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/f/6afeef1106de24c7bc3d2eb1e5b2b0a446362a67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + a^2 r^2 + a^2 r^4 + \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"170\" height=\"16\" />.  We know this series has sum  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/5/77596dddd5a5c21b8334e84fd87015b1db9c8a3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20050 = \\frac{a^2}{1 - r^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"119\" height=\"39\" />.  Dividing this equation by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/2/d92b8c5d55f66f20ed3f225d99a712796b2efced.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{1-r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"42\" height=\"33\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/9/279d11b5d97ae895f577d6c4e2972d92a0344bf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 = \\frac a{1 + r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"85\" height=\"34\" />.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/3/603d08c1921c121567bcf2c4e71f486fd139db93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 2005 - 2005r$\" width=\"136\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/c/a3c733b540354840297c31dc0fbc0b47619c4c67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 10 + 10r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/7/41704839a8ad57774546cb0cb4b5df36dd726fe3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2005 - 2005r = 10 + 10r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"194\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/e/b0e2900fbb6a6b0eb49e113e4b1b9d88be611da1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1995 = 2015r$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" /> and finally <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/8/2981dfc24a6d20c4d775203116e28708c55ef6b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac{1995}{2015} = \\frac{399}{403}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"127\" height=\"38\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/8/fe87aab6f6180438114f0cf55bd07a4f3a2512ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$399 + 403 = \\boxed{802}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"23\" />.  \n</p><p>(We know this last fraction is fully reduced by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Euclidean_algorithm\" title=\"Euclidean algorithm\">Euclidean algorithm</a> -- because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/a/eead0def7ac5b3fb2bd0b007cce347971525dd3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 = 403 - 399$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"109\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/4/b543692d483efa868938cb34ea03185451021a1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(403, 399) | 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" />.  But 403 is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Odd_integer\" title=\"Odd integer\"> odd</a>, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6ad52ed47cfacf8bc340ac150b6782303939242.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(403, 399) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"139\" height=\"20\" />.)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can write the sum of the original series as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/a/b5ad3da5e5776ce2f361c01a115380edcbd35b6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + a\\left(\\dfrac{m}{n}\\right) + a\\left(\\dfrac{m}{n}\\right)^2 + \\ldots = 2005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"272\" height=\"36\" />, where the common ratio is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/4/524d9b869d9ee2d8b923afa9ce7c2c36bd9489e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"18\" height=\"33\" />. We can also write the sum of the second series as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/d/e4d10dbb759efe2b6a4fa1fa76866ccbd80448d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + a^2\\left(\\dfrac{m}{n}\\right)^2 + a^2\\left(\\left(\\dfrac{m}{n}\\right)^2\\right)^2 + \\ldots = 20050$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"344\" height=\"46\" />. Using the formula for the sum of an infinite geometric series <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/e/cfe36225e9b4dbeaa57c7dd4cd3f6ed398876a02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=\\dfrac{a}{1-r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"79\" height=\"33\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is the sum of the sequence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the first term of the sequence, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the ratio of the sequence, the sum of the original series can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/6/c06d9ff2c8cd29999c4ad6a6cff099b88904566d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{a}{1-\\frac{m}{n}}=\\dfrac{a}{\\frac{n-m}{n}}=\\dfrac{a \\cdot n}{n-m}=2005\\;\\text{(1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"276\" height=\"39\" />, and the second sequence can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/6/3464ecd26dfaa87be4d75a2eb2db8a8e2daf35df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{a^2}{1-\\frac{m^2}{n^2}}=\\dfrac{a^2}{\\frac{n^2-m^2}{n^2}}=\\dfrac{a^2\\cdot n^2}{(n+m)(n-m)}=20050\\;\\text{(2)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"382\" height=\"46\" />. Dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/4/58473737c64d53e0635837ffc0526f79283e048e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(2)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/7/75773e8f8a9093e2c1ea3efb81ae6c0295a4041a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" />, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/6/946d5c4a83eebf4354012481a6cb1998e504a4ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{a\\cdot n}{m+n}=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"95\" height=\"34\" />, which can also be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/6/7165479adc786a07d38a72f65bf8146cd6f01646.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\cdot n=10(m+n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"138\" height=\"18\" />. Substitute this value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/e/1bed46df012a635ab016de5b669c064374b610ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\cdot n$\" width=\"33\" height=\"8\" /> back into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/7/75773e8f8a9093e2c1ea3efb81ae6c0295a4041a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" />, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/a/fba5b8a57378853862717bd7869b9f0fea331424.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\cdot \\dfrac{n+m}{n-m}=2005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"144\" height=\"35\" />. Dividing both sides by 10 yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/0/42048a2a18abfb6d28eab2287ff8fecbe37500d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{n+m}{n-m}=\\dfrac{401}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"107\" height=\"37\" /> we can now write a system of equations with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/7/857fce7741ae07736be88e89eb0b3c82cc512311.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+m=401$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"99\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/4/0742c13b380376b615f0238be96248888ba7ecd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-m=2$\" width=\"82\" height=\"12\" />, but this does not output integer solutions. However, we can also write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/0/42048a2a18abfb6d28eab2287ff8fecbe37500d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{n+m}{n-m}=\\dfrac{401}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"107\" height=\"37\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/7/dc751897e115bea91caaab5e89bbf9bb8a067650.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{n+m}{n-m}=\\dfrac{802}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"107\" height=\"38\" />. This gives the system of equations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/3/ee3b6a6fd64d72f25bba18a04df5845d37d45b21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n=802$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"100\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/e/78ece1f117665f01106cceafab80ac3089842977.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-m=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"12\" />, which does have integer solutions. Our answer is therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/a/65a374750dfcc105bce32bb3294871526e2b9520.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n=\\boxed{802}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" /> (Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/3/4f39a3242724f70e81d9037b59cca455b4794683.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$399$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/2/972c327fd113f3d2656df81653a53eeaea7f838c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$403$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, respectively, which are co-prime).\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An infinite geometric series has sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/5/9f5b442c275b4324f100c365b774e872b6b21f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2005$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" />. A new series, obtained by squaring each term of the original series, has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times the value of the original series. The common ratio of the original series is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db26f75f6218a382840f0ed34f5d36bcff61d33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Solution.\n</p><p>We write using the infinite geometric series formula, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> denoting the first term and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> denoting the common ratio. Thus, we have the two equations<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/b/22b82bccafb3a1944e619d11ef2636dc45effd5e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2005 = \\frac{a}{1-r}\\]\" width=\"102\" height=\"32\" />and<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/3/7c39406bdcfb67be775feaeea14ed5d3c44fde28.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[20050 = \\frac{a^2}{1-r^2}\\]\" width=\"118\" height=\"39\" />. Simping equation 2 using difference of squares gives<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/1/d9103a11c662aa3a6485c5491f5daf643dde6f0a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[20050 = \\frac{a}{1-r} \\times \\frac{a}{1+r}\\]\" width=\"178\" height=\"34\" />. Hmm, wink wink, you might think. We can substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/2/d92b8c5d55f66f20ed3f225d99a712796b2efced.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{1-r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"42\" height=\"33\" /> for 2005! This can simp down really easily! This gets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/7/bf7b434c0a21c9ee8a0ad8a273caad7f343db97b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 = \\frac{a}{1+r}!!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"98\" height=\"36\" /> Brilliant Move!\n</p><p>We then get the system of equations\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/b/f0bc1ec2bd9a8cb6499c79dc067383a8acdf16e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 = \\frac{a}{1+r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"88\" height=\"36\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/8/a886997d3a8c5046b2b5026b7a9813b6052bb801.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2005 = \\frac{a}{1-r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"106\" height=\"36\" />. Multiplying each side by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa92cd221f0657241decf09e72f5f0e5cde6ae8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/a/6ba89c43cfa9e8fe6bb14ec2e127cd2a600be3a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10(1+r)=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/2/6125ea675e841fd872202c0c248471929118211d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2005(1-r)=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" />! Equating both sides gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/d/79d1afee1aa4493f71c6f0379113f3bc282c277e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10+10r=2005-2005r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"197\" height=\"15\" />! By doing a little algebra, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/d/24dc3bcf1bd1807710e6bcabf956deb013c6436d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1995=2015r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/2/bd2da636b38df5fa7d0115507acb558ad893a3a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\frac{1995}{2015}!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"80\" height=\"38\" />\nThis then simps to 399 /403, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/5/905f0e87cf9e9d5036a600e76f1c46504a16d6dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{802}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/z4-bFo2D3TU?list=PLZ6lgLajy7SZ4MsF6ytXTrVOheuGNnsqn&amp;t=4500\">https://youtu.be/z4-bFo2D3TU?list=PLZ6lgLajy7SZ4MsF6ytXTrVOheuGNnsqn&amp;t=4500</a>\n- AMBRIGGS\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/3wNLfRyRrMo?t=383\">https://youtu.be/3wNLfRyRrMo?t=383</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II\" title=\"2005 AIME II\">2005 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2005\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017204147\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.049 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.072 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 456/100